### Active Battle Phase (20 seconds)
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#State-Updates#Battle-Timer
// - @battle-movement-system.mdc#Movement-Rules#Network-Lines

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Combat-Sequence#Attack-Initiation
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Feedback#State-Updates

- Battle Timer
  - Simple 20-second countdown display
  - Located at screen top
  - No intermediate warnings
  - Continuous countdown until completion
- Network Line Movement:
  - Battalions must stay on network lines when moving
  - Can traverse any connected network line to reach target
  - No restrictions on which lines can be used after initial attack
- Combat System:
  - Attack frequency determined solely by speed stat
  - Target selection based purely on proximity
  - State updates every 1 second for consistency
  - Visual updates synchronized with state timer
  - Begin attacks immediately when in range
  - Capture mechanics identical for all types
- Real-time feedback with batched updates

